# bizflow reads NO environment variables. There is no configuration file, no
# environment variable, and no credential of any kind.
#
# Everything it needs is either a command-line argument or a YAML file:
#
#   --templates DIR   invoice2data header templates
#                     default: ~/.local/share/invoice2data-templates,
#                     falling back to ./templates in the repo
#   --layout FILE     line-item column layout
#                     default: the bundled synthetic sample,
#                     bizflow/layouts/it.sample-vendor.yml
#   --out DIR         where process writes header/items/summary
#                     default: bizflow-out/
#
# The tool opens local files and prints to stdout. It makes no network calls.
# This file exists to say that explicitly, because the absence of a config
# surface is a fact worth stating rather than leaving a reader to infer.
